  "challenge": "The packet already decides this without a clerk: PR-001 is a HIGH overcharge against the contracted reference, the policy rationale is explicitly 'Overcharge relative to contracted price,' and the invoice carries no PO, quote, or note that would evidence an agreed uplift. Vendor history is empty (0 prior invoices) so there is no acceptance pattern to lean on, and get_prior_invoice shows INV-1014 was never seen before. WidgetA's 2.6% variance stayed inside tolerance and does not soften the WidgetB breach. With no documentary hook for a price change, the correct disposition is REJECT and request a corrected invoice or credit—not park it for manual confirmation of a fact the packet never supplies.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["PR-001"]
}
